# Backup wrapper logs are NOT managed by logrotate.
#
# Backup wrappers create pre-dated log files (e.g. diff-backup-YYYY-MM-DD.log),
# so logrotate's dateext approach would produce double-dated filenames.
# Compression and archival is handled instead by:
#   infra/backups/backups-log-archive.sh  (run daily via systemd timer)
#
# See also: infra/db/postgresql-log-archive.sh which uses the same approach.

